COMPOSITION
Use a warm ivory paper field with roughly one third calm negative space. Place exactly one large central chest-up portrait or frontal sculptural hero form across the lower two thirds. Split the supplied main headline into two tiers of enormous cobalt high-contrast Didone serif letters, wider than the canvas, partially cropped and alternately passing behind and in front of the subject. Add one small ruled numeric block at upper left and one compact right-aligned three-to-five-line editorial note at upper right. Recompose the hierarchy specifically for the requested aspect ratio; do not rotate or letterbox it.

TORN-PAPER STRUCTURE
Create exactly one broad irregular horizontal physical tear across the middle third. The bright white fibrous edges must be unmistakable. Inside the displaced strip reveal a case-specific detail such as hands, strings, plans, fabric, material, or motion; do not isolate or repeat the source eyes. The ripped strip must interrupt both the central image and portions of the headline.

TYPOGRAPHY
Render the supplied main headline as legible monumental cobalt Didone lettering with extreme thick-thin contrast, sharp serifs, and elegant open counters. Choose one short keyword from that new headline and repeat it once as a delicate copperplate-like cobalt italic crossing the torn band. Add two brief case-specific script labels near opposing lower corners. Keep microcopy restrained and use only the supplied text; no extra cover lines, brands, logos, or random pseudo-text.

COLOR, PHOTO, AND FINISH
Restrict graphic ink to saturated cobalt blue on warm ivory and paper white. Keep the natural photographic tones muted, warm, and subordinate. Photograph the subject frontally with diffuse low-contrast light, minimal depth, and believable anatomy or material form. Apply visible controlled newspaper halftone, scan grain, paper tooth, and slight print softness without destroying text or facial detail. All layers are flat printed collage; use no realistic drop shadow, bevel, glossy depth, or presentation mockup.

AVOID
No copied face, eye strip, hairstyle, shirt, source words, source date, source layout coordinates, or future-vision premise. No multiple subjects, scenic environment, stickers, scrapbook clutter, comic panels, sans-serif headline, slab serif, gradients, extra saturated inks, glossy commercial retouching, 3D type, glow, lens flare, extreme degradation, illegible headline, malformed anatomy, duplicated features, watermark, signature, username, QR code, platform UI, or logo.

Important content rule: match the sparse cobalt Didone, centered halftone portrait, one-rip editorial system first; then replace the source identity, gesture, prop, setting, text, and story premise with the new case content.

